          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "The task is complete. I fixed the resource leak in shell completion by properly closing file contexts in the `_resolve_context` function in `src/click/shell_completion.py`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem**: Click was not properly closing file options during shell completion, causing `ResourceWarning` messages when CLI commands used `click.File()` with shell completion enabled. The contexts created during shell completion were never closed because `__exit__` was never called.\n\n**Solution**: Wrapped all context creation calls in `_resolve_context` with proper `with` statements to ensure automatic cleanup:\n\n1. Main context: `with cli.make_context(...) as ctx:`\n2. Sub-context for non-chained groups: `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_ctx:`\n3. Sub-context for chained groups: `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_sub_ctx:`\n\nThis ensures all file handles and resources managed by contexts are properly cleaned up during shell completion.\n\n**Files Modified**:\n- `src/click/shell_completion.py` - Updated `_resolve_context` function (lines 547-590)\n\n**Verification**:\n- All 40 shell completion tests pass\n- Custom resource leak tests confirm no `ResourceWarning` for simple commands, groups, nested groups, and chained groups with file options\n- 558 tests pass overall (excluding `test_basic.py` which has a pre-existing pytest compatibility issue unrelated to this change)",
