          "final_text_tail": " no timeout \u2713\n- close() enforces the timeout and logs a warning \u2713\n- shell completion respects the timeout (ctx_args flow + closing the resolved ctx) \u2713\n\nDone. Task complete.\n\nImplementation is complete and verified:\n\n**`src/click/core.py`**\n- Added `cleanup_timeout: float | None = None` parameter to `Context.__init__` (src/click/core.py:291), with validation raising `ValueError` for zero/negative values; stored as `self.cleanup_timeout`.\n- `Context.close()` (src/click/core.py:624) now runs the exit stack cleanup in a daemon thread when a timeout is set, joins with the timeout budget, and on expiry prints a warning to stderr and abandons the hung cleanup (remaining callbacks are skipped); exceptions from completed callbacks still propagate. `None` keeps the original synchronous behavior.\n\n**`src/click/shell_completion.py`**\n- `ShellComplete.get_completions` now closes the resolved context in a `finally` block, so cleanup registered during completion runs and honors `cleanup_timeout` (passed via `ctx_args` \u2192 `make_context` \u2192 `Context`). Shell completion can no longer hang on unresponsive cleanup.\n\n**`CHANGES.rst`** \u2014 added changelog entry.\n\nVerified: validation errors, timeout enforcement (hanging callback abandoned in ~0.5s with warning), normal cleanup within budget, no-timeout behavior unchanged, completion accepting/validating `cleanup_timeout`, and full test suite passes (614 passed, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed; one pre-existing pytest collection warning unrelated to the change).",
